Convert in the one directory a payload has, rather than a temp dir

`CallZapd` builds a scratch directory, symlinks the install's `assets` into it and
chdirs there, so a desktop can run the extractor from somewhere writable without
disturbing the install. Every part of that is a desktop assumption, and on this
platform each one fails differently:

  - `temp_directory_path()` reads TMPDIR and falls back to `/tmp`. A payload's
    sandbox has neither, so the scratch directory is made somewhere that is not
    there.
  - `create_symlink` reaches `common/posix`'s `symlink`, which refuses - see
    `common/posix/include/fcntl.h`. `std::filesystem` reports that by throwing,
    which ends the conversion before ZAPD is reached.
  - `current_path(tempdir)` reaches `chdir`, which answers and changes nothing. A
    payload has one directory and cannot move it, so even a scratch directory that
    existed would never be entered.

None of it is needed. A payload has exactly one directory, `/app0`, which is both
the install and where the archive belongs, and the relative paths this function
already builds - `assets/xml/<version>`, `assets/filelists`, `--otrfile oot.o2r` -
resolve against it at the kernel boundary. So this reads the definitions where
`shim/soh_start.c` unpacked them and writes `oot.o2r` beside them, first time.

The copy at the end goes with it. `otrFile` and `exportdir` both resolve to
`/app0`, so it is a file onto itself, and `std::filesystem::copy` calls equivalent
paths an error rather than a no-op.

diff --git a/soh/soh/Extractor/Extract.cpp b/soh/soh/Extractor/Extract.cpp
index 93fa64c..fa82a74 100644
--- a/soh/soh/Extractor/Extract.cpp
+++ b/soh/soh/Extractor/Extract.cpp
@@ -662,6 +662,23 @@ bool Extractor::CallZapd(std::string installPath, std::string exportdir, std::at
     std::string romPath = std::filesystem::absolute(mCurrentRomPath).string();
     installPath = std::filesystem::absolute(installPath).string();
     exportdir = std::filesystem::absolute(exportdir).string();
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    // No scratch directory, because there is nothing for one to solve here.
+    //
+    // The temporary directory below exists so a desktop can run the extractor from
+    // somewhere writable without disturbing the install, and it is built out of three
+    // things this platform does not have: a temp directory (`temp_directory_path` reads
+    // TMPDIR and falls back to /tmp, and a payload's sandbox holds neither), a symlink
+    // (`common/posix`'s `symlink` refuses, so the call throws), and a working directory
+    // that can move (`chdir` answers and changes nothing - see `common/posix/posix.c`).
+    //
+    // What it needs instead is already true. A payload has exactly one directory, /app0,
+    // which is both the install and the place the archive belongs; the relative paths
+    // just below resolve against it at the kernel boundary, which is what
+    // `oops_fs_resolve_path` is for. So `assets/xml/...` reads the definitions unpacked
+    // by `shim/soh_start.c` and `--otrfile oot.o2r` writes beside them, first time.
+    (void)exportdir;
+#else
     // Work this out in the temporary folder
     std::string tempdir = Mkdtemp();
     std::string curdir = std::filesystem::current_path().string();
@@ -673,6 +690,7 @@ bool Extractor::CallZapd(std::string installPath, std::string exportdir, std::at
 #endif
 
     std::filesystem::current_path(tempdir);
+#endif
 
     snprintf(xmlPath, 1024, "assets/xml/%s", version);
     snprintf(confPath, 1024, "assets/Config_%s.xml", version);
@@ -703,11 +721,17 @@ bool Extractor::CallZapd(std::string installPath, std::string exportdir, std::at
 
     zapd_report(argc, (char**)argv.data(), extractCount, totalExtract);
 
+#ifndef __PROSPERO__
     std::filesystem::copy(otrFile, exportdir + "/" + otrFile, std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
 
     // Go back to where this game was executed from
     std::filesystem::current_path(curdir);
     std::filesystem::remove_all(tempdir);
+#endif
+    // On this platform the copy above would be a file onto itself: `otrFile` and
+    // `exportdir` both resolve to /app0, so ZAPD has already written it where
+    // libultraship will look, and `std::filesystem::copy` treats equivalent paths as an
+    // error rather than a no-op.
 
     return false;
 }
